        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4a82e71f3ed84f33aa256922a706d47e",
      "statement": "When version.RequireClientAuthentication is true an x509 identity CSR is created, and host identity certs prepend a URI SAN (the code expects the uuid URI first); the UUID comes from --host-id machine (blake2b of /etc/machine-id keyed with 'man moon machine', formatted as v4), an explicit UUID, reuse of an existing identity cert's UUID so reruns don't clobber the host ID, or a fresh random UUID.",
      "evidence": [
